# Test: the TFTP server reports a clear error and does NOT claim "started" when
# no interface binds -- the install-path silent-failure class.
# VALIDATES: the tftpserver zero-listener guard: a bind failure on every
#            configured interface yields "no interfaces bound" instead of a
#            false "tftpserver: started".
# PREVENTS: regression of the silent bind-failure that left the install servers
#           logging "started" while serving nothing (the original PXE failure).
#
# Mechanism: listen-interface names a device that does not exist. On Linux
# SO_BINDTODEVICE rejects the bind, so every interface fails and the guard fires.
# INFO logging is enabled so a regressed "started" line would appear (and trip
# the reject).
#
# needs-linux: other platforms ignore the interface and bind the port globally
# (no SO_BINDTODEVICE), so the failure cannot be forced portably; the unit-level
# bindDeviceFor coverage applies on every platform.
option=needs-linux

stdin=ze-tftp:terminator=EOF_CONF
service {
    tftp-server {
        enabled true
        listen-interface ze-no-such-iface0
        root-directory /var/lib/tftp
        max-transfers 10
    }
}
EOF_CONF

option=env:var=ze.log.tftpserver:value=info

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-tftp
# The await fence holds the daemon until its relayed stderr carries the needle,
# replacing the blind hold that guessed how long that took. The needle carries no
# ':' because parseAwait kv-splits the value, so it starts after any log prefix;
# the expect below still asserts the full phrase. The exit-code expectation is
# gone because awaitDaemonStderr owns the wait arm in runner_exec.go, so it could
# never fire. Every stderr assertion is unchanged.
# Producer: tftpserver/register.go, "tftpserver: no interfaces bound; server
# not serving".
await=stderr:contains=no interfaces bound
expect=stderr:contains=no interfaces bound
reject=stderr:pattern=tftpserver: started
